<p>I think you hit upon my issue with the piece by way of this explanation. If this is an introduction to things that haven't happened yet, why am I not reading about those things? They sound interesting. But I can't read about those things here, because this isn't actually a story, it's a chapter in a larger narrative.</p>
<p>The article conveys what La Rue Macabre and Darkwater Lodge are, but it relies too much on my pre-existing knowledge to make me care. Is shit about to pop off? I don't know, because I'm expected to be familiar with both GOIs to know the significance of La Rue not liking the Foundation anymore.</p>
<p>Again, I don't want to insinuate that this is poorly written. That's clearly not the case! But I feel that an article should act as a standalone piece, and I do not feel this does that.</p>

